# Baked Ziti

{ rating="4" image="baked_ziti.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] [Ziti noodles]{ ing="ziti-noodles" }
- [ ] 6 oz [spinach]{ ing="spinach" }
- [ ] 1 jar (1 pound 9 ounces) [pasta sauce]{ ing="pasta-sauce" }
- [ ] 1 cup [ricotta cheese]{ ing="ricotta-cheese" }
- [ ] 1[⁄2 cup Parmesan]{ ing="2-cup-parmesan" }
- [ ] 1[⁄2 tsp garlic powder]{ ing="2-tsp-garlic-powder" }
- [ ] 1[⁄4 tsp black pepper]{ ing="4-tsp-black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1 cup [shredded mozzarella]{ ing="shredded-mozzarella" }, divided

## Recipe

1. Prepare pasta according to the instructions
1. Add [spinach]{ ing="spinach" } during the last minute of cook time, then drain the pasta and spinach. Place back in the pot
1. Stir the [pasta sauce]{ ing="pasta-sauce" }, ricotta, [Parmesan]{ ing="2-cup-parmesan" }, garlic, [black pepper]{ ing="4-tsp-black-pepper" }, and 1⁄2 cup [mozzarella]{ ing="shredded-mozzarella" }
1. Spoon pasta mixture into 9x13 inch pan and sprinkle the remaining 1/2 cup of [mozzarella]{ ing="shredded-mozzarella" } on top
1. Bake at 350 degrees for 30 min

## Notes

1. If put in the fridge, extend cook time by 10-15 min!
1. Alex’s family recipe and great for groups
